# --- CRMA / Wave bloat (org has CRMA enabled) ---
# When CRM Analytics for Nonprofit Cloud / Fundraising Cloud is enabled in the
# source org, a plain `sf project retrieve start` pulls ~100+ Wave/CRMA components
# that are not owned by FQS. Ignore the entire family so the repo stays clean.
# NOTE: **/contentassets/** is NOT ignored globally — a broad ContentAsset ignore
# would drop legitimate assets. If Wave-scoped ContentAssets leak into retrieves,
# they live under the wave* paths below and are already filtered.
**/waveApplications/**
**/waveComponents/**
**/waveDashboards/**
**/waveDatasets/**
**/waveLenses/**
**/waveRecipes/**
**/waveTemplateBundles/**
**/waveXmds/**
**/wave/**

# --- Agentforce companion metadata ---
# Every FQS flow deployed against an Agentforce-enabled org generates a matching
# GenOpAgentConfig ("Gen Op Agent Config") metadata file — 1:1 twin noise the
# accelerator does not own. Ignore the folder so retrieves don't pull it back in.
# genAi* companions (genAiPlanners / genAiPlugins / genAiFunctions) have not been
# observed in this repo's retrieves yet; the globs below are prophylactic.
**/genOpAgentConfigs/**
**/genAiPlanners/**
**/genAiPlugins/**
**/genAiFunctions/**

# --- SFDX retrieve noise ---
# Full-profile retrieves pull hundreds of standard-object field references that
# have nothing to do with FQS. Ignore all profiles as a class — FQS delivers
# permission sets, not profiles. (The Admin.profile-meta.xml line above is now
# redundant but kept for clarity.)
**/profiles/**

# Orphan email templates: unfiled$public is a legitimate Salesforce folder for
# templates authored outside a Public folder. FQS_Gift_Acknowledgement lives here
# by design, so we do NOT ignore the whole folder — leaving this comment as a
# reminder that noise in unfiled$public should be reviewed, not globbed away.

# PermissionSetGroup for the force__* namespace is Salesforce-managed platform
# noise; the specific pattern is already covered above under "Non-FQS permission
# sets…". Keeping this comment as a marker so future contributors know it lives
# there and shouldn't be duplicated here.

# BatchCalcJobDefinitions: no auto-modified definitions have been observed in
# this repo yet. If a future retrieve pulls one, add:
#   **/batchCalcJobDefinitions/**
# below this comment. Left as a placeholder pending evidence.

# Standard-object field noise: if you find yourself repeatedly adding standard
# field-meta.xml paths to this file, scope your retrieve instead. Use
# `sf project retrieve start -m <MetadataType>:<ApiName>` with an explicit list
# rather than a full-object retrieve — that way you never pull the noise in the
# first place.
